        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: царапина",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "царапина (tsarápina) — \"a scratch\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "После игры с кошкой у меня на руке царапина. Pósle igrý s kóshkoy u menyá na ruké tsarápina. After playing with the cat I've got a scratch on my hand."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. The verb is царапать / поцарапать — to scratch."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "царапина (tsarápina) is built on царапать 'to scratch', which EtymDB lists without a source; it is usually taken as imitative."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
